ClaimStepLog TABLE (Azure SQL)
──────────────────────────────────────────────
ClaimId        UNIQUEIDENTIFIER  NOT NULL
StepName       VARCHAR(50)       NOT NULL  -- 'DocumentValidation'
CompletedAt    DATETIME2         NOT NULL
Result         NVARCHAR(MAX)     NULL      -- JSON result payload
DurationMs     INT               NOT NULL
PRIMARY KEY (ClaimId, StepName)

IDEMPOTENT STEP EXECUTION PATTERN
──────────────────────────────────────────────
async Task<StepResult> ExecuteStepAsync(
  string claimId, string stepName,
  Func<Task<StepResult>> stepLogic)
{
  // 1. Check checkpoint
  var existing = await _db.ClaimStepLog
    .FirstOrDefaultAsync(x =>
      x.ClaimId == claimId &&
      x.StepName == stepName);

  if (existing != null)
  {
    // Step already completed — return cached result
    // Fraud API not called again. No double billing.
    return JsonSerializer
      .Deserialize<StepResult>(existing.Result);
  }

  // 2. Execute the step
  var result = await stepLogic();

  // 3. Record completion atomically
  await _db.ClaimStepLog.AddAsync(new ClaimStepLog {
    ClaimId = claimId,
    StepName = stepName,
    CompletedAt = DateTime.UtcNow,
    Result = JsonSerializer.Serialize(result)
  });
  await _db.SaveChangesAsync();

  return result;
}

REDELIVERY SCENARIO — Step 4 Failed
──────────────────────────────────────────────
First delivery:
Step 1 DocumentValidation  → executes → logged ✓
Step 2 FraudScoring        → executes → logged ✓
Step 3 PolicyVerification  → executes → logged ✓
Step 4 PaymentSettlement   → CRASH (processor dies)
Message lock expires → redelivered

Second delivery (same ClaimId):
Step 1 DocumentValidation  → checkpoint hit → SKIP ✓
Step 2 FraudScoring        → checkpoint hit → SKIP ✓
Step 3 PolicyVerification  → checkpoint hit → SKIP ✓
Step 4 PaymentSettlement   → no checkpoint → executes
                           → logged ✓
                           → message.CompleteAsync()

Fraud API called: 1 time (not 2)
Bank transfer triggered: 1 time (not 2)
Hospital paid: exactly once
